WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:06.020
Moana is packed with Disney and movie easter
eggs from Big Hero 6 to Zootopia, Frozen and

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.850
The Little Mermaid all the way through to
Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.380
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to explain all

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.380
the easter eggs, hidden mickeys, in-jokes
and movie references I found in Moana.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.019
Just before I start, I've got a very cool
giveaway for this awesome The Art of Moana

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:26.830
hardback book which features beautiful concept
art from the movie and fascinating details

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.199
about the making of the film.

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:32.509
For a chance to win, just subscribe and leave
a comment about the easter eggs on this video

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.150
or let me know about any other easter eggs
you spotted.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.620
And as an extra thank-you to you for watching
this video, there's also some bonus ways to

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.800
enter the giveaway via the Gleam link in the
video description below!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.860
Ok, quick warning: there are spoilers ahead
for the movie, so if you want to avoid those,

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.910
you check out my spoiler-free review of Moana
right here.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.260
Moana directors Ron Clements and John Musker
are veteran Disney creators and there are

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.410
a bunch of easter eggs to their previous films
at Disney in Moana.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.430
Let's start with The Little Mermaid because
there's some hidden symbolism in the locket

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.220
which Gramma Tala gives Moana that contains
the Heart of Te Fiti.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.640
The heart and the locket call back to Ursula's
enchanted necklace which held Ariel's voice

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.700
captive and just as The Little Mermaid's story
is only resolved when Ariel's voice is restored

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.420
to her, so too Moana resolves her story by
restoring the Heart to Te Kā at the end of

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:20.420
the movie.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.890
The circular swirl of the shell on Ursula's
necklace is also reflected in the circular

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.520
swirly symbolism scattered throughout Moana
such as on the gem itself, the ship sails,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.120
the rock that Maui prised the Heart of Te
Fiti from, and the circular sand pattern when

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.940
the gem first reveals itself to Moana.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.690
When Maui traps Moana in a cave with a huge
statue of himself at the end of his song "You're

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:46.230
Welcome", it's a nod to the statue of Prince
Eric that Ariel kept in her cave.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.770
Later when Maui's statue topples over as Moana
uses it to climb out of the cave, a broken

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:55.120
piece from Maui's face, his nose, in fact,
bounces up into the screen, which is a little

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.630
hat tip to both the broken piece of Eric's
statue that was used to win Ariel over for

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.730
Ursula, and to the moment in Aladdin when
Jasmine and Aladdin fly by the pyramids on

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:08.030
the magic carpet and disturb one of the sculptors
who chips off the nose of an enormous sphinx

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.030
statue.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.990
And, by the way, there's a neat parallel between
Ariel and Moana in that both their fathers

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.400
want them to stay within the limits of their
worlds: King Triton doesn't want Ariel to

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.810
go ashore and Chief Tui won't allow Moana
beyond the reef.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:26.170
And Moana's story is like Ariel's in reverse
as Moana longs to leave the land for the sea,

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.830
while Ariel longs to leave the sea for the
land.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.860
Plus, there's a nice nod to Ariel's hair flower
in the pink flower Moana wears in her hair.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.319
And in the movie's end credits scene, there's
a brilliant shout-out to the crab Sebastian

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:41.310
from The Little Mermaid as well as a dig at
his accent.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:45.430
In the scene, Tamatoa appears and he's still
stuck upside down on his back.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.500
He pokes fun at himself and his "Shiny" song
and then says to the audience, "Still upside

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.500
down here!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.130
Just need a little push!", before pausing
and then adding, "Can we be real?

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:58.430
If my name was Sebastian and I had a cool
Jamaican accent, you'd totally help me!

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.580
You would, you know you would!"

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.620
Moana's directors have also confirmed that
Ariel's sidekick, Flounder, appears in Moana

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.040
and I think I spotted him among the fish which
appear during the 2D animation section of

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.319
Maui's "You're Welcome" song.

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:16.290
As you can expect, there are some nice Frozen
easter eggs in the film, so make sure you

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:21.810
pay attention in Tamatoa's lair after Maui
recovers his fishhook as the demi-god has

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.640
difficulty shapeshifting and accidentally
switches into a number of different animals,

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.270
and one of them, which flashes by, is none
other than Kristoff's reindeer, Sven.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:34.900
Clements and Musker also directed Aladdin,
and Maui's rapid shapeshifting into different

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.590
creatures in this scene tips its hat to the
Genie's fast and humorous transformations

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:43.480
as well as the various quick and funny transformations
that Aladdin's monkey Abu goes through.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.750
And when Moana wakes up on Maui's island after
being ship-wrecked, her hair is all messed

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:52.330
up and full of sand, which is a nod to when
Anna woke up with big messed-up hair in Frozen.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:57.750
As I'm sure you remember, snowman Olaf actually
loves summer and likes to imagine himself

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.230
sunbathing on the beach.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.780
Now, we don't actually see him soaking up
the sun in Moana, as you can imagine what

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.670
would happen to him if he did that, but Moana's
directors have said that he is hidden in the

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:11.640
film, so keep your eyes peeled for what would
be left of a snowman if he went in the sun,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.440
for example, his carrot nose.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.930
And Moana screenwriter, Jared Bush, pokes
a bit of fun at the idea of Disney princesses

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:24.009
when Moana states that she is not a princess,
but Maui replies that, "If you wear a dress

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:26.860
and you have an animal sidekick, you're a
princess."

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:32.440
Moana's directors are also behind Disney's
1997 animated feature, Hercules, so it's intriguing

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.479
that Maui's backstory is a reverse of Hercules'
backstory.

00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:40.759
Maui was a mortal who was abandoned by his
human parents and taken in by gods who made

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:41.759
him a demi-god.

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:46.379
But Hercules, however, had gods as parents
but ended up being raised by humans after

00:04:46.379 --> 00:04:48.300
he was abandoned on earth by Hades' minions.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:53.129
And, in a nice bit of coincidence, Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson, who's the voice of Maui,

00:04:53.129 --> 00:04:59.729
also played the role of Hercules in the 2014
live-action movie of the same name.

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:04.460
The funny line where Maui interrupts Moana
as she's addressing him as "Maui, shapeshifter,

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:08.349
demi-god of the wind and sea" and he tells
her that she needs to add "Hero of Men…

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:12.539
and Women" to her list of epithets for him
could be a nod to the moniker of "The People's

00:05:12.539 --> 00:05:16.169
Champion" that Dwayne Johnson took on during
his wrestling days.

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:20.699
Mini-Maui, who's Maui's tattoo sidekick and
acts as the demi-god's conscience, brings

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:24.719
to mind the character of Jiminy Cricket, who
was the conscience of Pinocchio in Disney's

00:05:24.719 --> 00:05:26.210
famous film from 1940.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:31.389
There's an amusing pop culture reference to
Twitter when Maui grabs Heihei and uses his

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:36.139
beak to sign Moana's oar saying that, "When
you use a bird to write with, it's called

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:37.139
tweeting."

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:41.809
And when Moana lands on top of Maui as they
jump into the Realm of Monsters, it's an interesting

00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:45.729
call-back with a twist to The Princess And
The Frog, which was made by Moana directors

00:05:45.729 --> 00:05:47.129
Clements and Musker.

00:05:47.129 --> 00:05:51.490
In this film, Maui lands first and thinks
he's all OK, but then Moana comes crashing

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:52.819
down on top of him.

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:56.870
And in The Princess And The Frog, Tiana and
Naveen are suspended in air by some balloons

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.990
which burst sending Tiana crashing down first.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.039
She's caught by a spider's web and thinks
she's safe, until Naveen comes crashing down

00:06:04.039 --> 00:06:05.539
on top of her.

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:10.319
And it's in Lalotai where we're introduced
to Tamatoa, the huge self-absorbed crab who

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:14.319
likes to collect and adorn himself with hundreds
of shiny objects.

00:06:14.319 --> 00:06:18.469
The character is reminiscent of The Collector
in Marvel's movies, who's portrayed by Benecio

00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:24.129
del Toro, and, like Tamatoa, is a shady character
who likes to collect special objects.

00:06:24.129 --> 00:06:27.819
There's also a hint of The Hobbit's dragon
Smaug, specifically Peter Jackson's film The

00:06:27.819 --> 00:06:32.569
Desolation of Smaug, about Tamatoa in the
way they both cover themselves in the hordes

00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:36.659
of treasure they've amassed in their lair
deep within a mountain, and in the way that,

00:06:36.659 --> 00:06:41.289
at first, both Bilbo Baggins and Moana don't
even realise they're walking on top of Smaug

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:45.879
and Tamatoa until the creatures emerge from
underneath their treasure.

00:06:45.879 --> 00:06:51.379
Tamatoa's fantastic song "Shiny" is heavily
influenced by David Bowie, and Jemaine Clement,

00:06:51.379 --> 00:06:55.839
who voices the enormous crab, actually played
David Bowie in an episode of his TV comedy

00:06:55.839 --> 00:06:57.589
series Flight of the Conchords.

00:06:57.589 --> 00:07:02.249
As Tamatoa raises himself up in his lair,
a number of shiny artefacts that he's been

00:07:02.249 --> 00:07:06.779
collecting fall off him and one of them looks
suspiciously like a rocket, which could be

00:07:06.779 --> 00:07:11.740
a nod to Disney's 1991 adventure movie, The
Rocketeer, which they're currently developing

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.189
a sequel to.

00:07:13.189 --> 00:07:18.319
The monsters that we see glimpses of in Lalotai
originate from Polynesian legends of Maui.

00:07:18.319 --> 00:07:22.050
For example, there's an eight-eyed bat who
Maui once killed when the bat tried to steal

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.069
Maui's wife Kumu-lama.

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:27.929
And there was a giant eel which represents
the eel god Tuna-roa, which Maui has killed

00:07:27.929 --> 00:07:29.460
in various legends.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:33.779
The Kakamora sequence is a cross between Gremlins
and Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:07:33.779 --> 00:07:37.990
In fact, the directors have said they specifically
wanted to pay homage to director George Miller

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.530
and his critically acclaimed Mad Max sequel.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:44.179
And there's a moment when Moana lands on the
deck of one of the Kakamora boats and they

00:07:44.179 --> 00:07:46.559
all suddenly turn and face her.

00:07:46.559 --> 00:07:51.599
Well, hidden among the Kakamora is a very
crafty easter egg to the lovable robot Baymax

00:07:51.599 --> 00:07:53.009
from Big Hero 6.

00:07:53.009 --> 00:07:57.949
Moana directors Ron Clements and John Musker
have cameo'd in many of their previous Disney

00:07:57.949 --> 00:08:01.689
films, and it looks like they might be hidden
among the Kakamora too.

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:05.620
If you stay through the whole credits, you'll
not only get to see the awesome Tamatoa post-credits

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:10.309
scene, but you'll also get to see a visual
shoutout to Disney's next animated feature,

00:08:10.309 --> 00:08:11.569
Wreck-It Ralph 2.

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:15.779
Just make sure you watch the little tapestries
that scroll by during the credits as there's

00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:20.149
a Wreck-It Ralph picture in one them, on the
right-hand side of the screen, right towards

00:08:20.149 --> 00:08:21.719
the end of the movie.

00:08:21.719 --> 00:08:25.679
And given that there were a number of Moana
easter eggs in Zootopia, it's hardly surprising

00:08:25.679 --> 00:08:30.149
to find an easter egg to Disney's last animated
hit in Moana, especially since the two films

00:08:30.149 --> 00:08:31.619
were written by Jared Bush.

00:08:31.619 --> 00:08:36.270
Remember in Zootopia there was a very funny
Moana easter egg via the Meowana bootlegged

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:38.750
Blu-ray that Weaselton was selling on his
stall.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:42.390
And there was also an easter egg to Maui's
fishhook on the back of Finnick's van.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:47.050
Well, the Zootopia easter egg in Moana takes
the form of the slow-talking, fast-driving

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.540
sloth, Flash.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.820
Moana's directors have said that Flash appears
in disguise which makes this creature here,

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:56.790
who appears in the Realm of Monsters sequence,
a very good candidate to be Flash.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.700
Notice he's got four claws, like Flash's,
on each limb.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:05.391
When the ocean first reaches out to Moana
as a sentient character in the movie, it's

00:09:05.391 --> 00:09:11.260
reminiscent of the alien water tentacle from
James Cameron's 1989 sci-fi movie The Abyss.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:16.430
And the ocean also has a sense of Aladdin's
magic carpet about it, in that it's a non-speaking

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:20.190
character that helps out Moana and guides
her forward in her quest.

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.880
There's a nod to Pixar's Crush and Squirt
in the scenes with toddler Moana when she's

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:28.300
on the beach and helps a baby turtle like
Squirt across the sand safely to the water;

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:32.510
and the baby turtle also swims by later with
a much larger turtle, who's similar to Crush

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.070
from Finding Nemo and Finding Dory.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:39.010
And that lovely moment when toddler Moana
gently takes a leaf and uses it to shield

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.770
the baby turtle to help it to the sea is also
a little easter egg to the photo of Stitch

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.550
doing the same during the credits of Lilo
&amp; Stitch.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:48.140
And there's another hat tip to Lilo &amp; Stitch
when Moana gets embarrassed about eating pork

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:52.410
in front of her pet pig Pua, which calls to
mind Lilo explaining why she couldn't feed

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:55.640
a tuna sandwich to her pet fish Pudge.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.570
There's also a recurring in-joke about eating
Heihei, for example, one of the villagers

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:03.690
wants to cook him as he thinks the rooster
is too stupid to survive, which is a reference

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:07.950
to the fact that Heihei was almost scrapped
from Moana as the filmmakers were struggling

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.040
to make the character work in the story.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.370
In fact, the day they figured out how to keep
Heihei in the movie, they all celebrated with

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:19.040
a meal of fried chicken, which means that
Moana eating pork in front of Pua is also

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.770
another in-joke about this!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:25.130
After Te Fiti's heart is returned, there's
a sequence where the mother island is restored

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:29.470
to life and in these shots of the island's
vegetation, there's what looks like the magical

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.340
golden flower from Tangled.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:36.340
Which seems very appropriate as the magical
flower is associated with healing and life.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:40.420
The character of Gramma Tala, whose spirit
becomes a ray in the ocean, is analogous to

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:44.930
Grandmother Willow in Pocahontas in that she
serves as a voice of wisdom and as someone

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.460
who can guide the young heroine of the story.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.690
And Gramma Tala's question to Moana "is there
something you want to hear?", which basically

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:56.310
means that Moana already knows her heritage
and what she should do, is an echo of Willow's

00:10:56.310 --> 00:11:01.350
advice to Pocahontas to listen to the spirits
and Willow's words that 'you know your path,

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.850
child, now follow it.'

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:07.780
By the way, there's a nod back to the brilliant
short Inner Workings which plays before Moana

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:12.010
when Moana yells at the ocean that "Fish pee
in you all day", and also when she thinks

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:16.330
she's found a warm current in the sea, but
it's actually because Maui's just pee'd in

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.330
it.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.280
If you remember, in Inner Workings, there's
a funny moment when the main character Paul

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:25.240
runs into the sea and we see his bladder give
a big smile and sigh, a cheeky joke about

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.170
Paul peeing in the sea.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:33.780
There is a nice Hidden Mickey that you can
see just briefly in the scene which introduces

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:35.130
us to Tamatoa and his lair.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:40.090
There are 3 pearls positioned on the sand
just below Tamatoa that look like the classic

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.320
Mickey Mouse silhouette.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:46.030
You can also see a similar Mickey on the character
poster for Tamatoa in the positioning of 3

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.850
pearls in a canoe to the right of Tamatoa.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.840
And there seem to be a few hidden mickeys
snuck in to the Kakamora scenes.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:56.641
They're a little difficult to spot among all
the action going on during their attack, but

00:11:56.641 --> 00:11:58.520
here are a few (possible) ones I spotted.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:02.920
In this shot, there seems to be a pair of
hidden Mickeys in the barrels or drums stacked

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.920
up on one of the Kakamora boats.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:09.110
Each mickey has two Kakamora standing on top
of what would be the ears in the mickey.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:13.410
And the way these coconuts are stacked also
look like another hidden mickey.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:18.060
I'm sure there are more hidden secrets tucked
away in these manically busy Kakamora scenes

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:19.890
that we'll have to wait for the Blu-ray to
spot!

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:24.070
Now, I'd love to know what other easter eggs
and references you spotted that I missed!

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.560
And how does Moana compare with your other
favourite Disney movies?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.400
Let me know in the comments below!

